```c
bitwise_copy(&c->value, sizeof c->value, 0, ...);
```

This copies `sizeof c->value` bytes from `c->value`. If `c->value` was allocated with xmalloc but only partially set (e.g., the lexer only sets some bytes), this could trigger MSAN.

